      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note",
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## 3d/multi-image-asset\n\nFour stills of one object (front, side, back, top-down) -> one textured mesh, so an asset is fused from several views instead of hallucinated from one.\n\nSources: four `LoadImage` nodes, each gated, unloaded, and run through its own `Trellis2Conditioning`. The four views share ONE `Trellis2ShapeStage`: the front view conditions the structure stage, the side view the shape stage, the back view the upsample stage, and the top-down view the texture pass. Four shape stages would be four separate meshes, so the lane fuses inside one.\n\nUNET: `trellis_2_int8_convrot.safetensors`. CLIP vision: `dino_v3_vit_l.safetensors` (DINOv3 license, opt-in pack). Structure decode stays at 32.\n\nUpsample `target_resolution` is an int and ComfyUI only accepts 1024-2048 in steps of 128; this graph runs the 1024 floor.\n\nBatch stays 1 and the mesh converts through MeshToFile3D, which keeps only batch item 0. SaveGLB writes the mesh to `output/assets/objects/_lab-multiview/asset_NNNNN_.glb`; MeshToFile3D only converts in memory. Do not mint an Asset Bible row from this graph.\n\nQueue `3d/world-elements` next to place the fused asset in a set.\n\nDINOv3 is Meta's custom commercial-friendly license - not Apache. MIT TRELLIS weights without DINOv3 cannot Queue.\n\nOccupancy: trellis - stop Blender desk, LTX, Wan, Klein denoise. One GB10 job.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Operator note"
    },
